From: dagu
Subject: [PATCH] dagu: do not stall KMS on the Cogl sync_fd; keep DISABLE_IMPLICIT_SYNC

Against mutter 50.1 (Ubuntu libmutter-18 50.1-0ubuntu2.2).

do_handle_update() on sync_fd>=0:

  1. sets META_KMS_ASSIGN_PLANE_FLAG_DISABLE_IMPLICIT_SYNC
  2. if the fd is not readable, register_fd() and sleep

On SM8250 the Cogl "latest" sync_file often stays unread 70-250 ms
while gpu_busy is already 0. Sleeping there delays drmHandleEvent.

The first live knife jumped straight to update_ready and skipped (1).
Atomic then has no IN_FENCE_FD (the property is only added when
DISABLE_IMPLICIT_SYNC is set, and the fd used is a signaled dummy,
never the Cogl fd). The kernel falls back to implicit GEM wait on
the GBM BO — same stale reservation, now as B-kick: maybe_post on
time, dpu_enc_kickoff +100-250 ms.

Keep (1), drop (2). Always update_ready once DISABLE is set.

Live ELF:
  0x1bd9ac  keep tbnz w20,#31,update_ready
  0x1bd9d8  g_poll setup  ->  b update_ready

---
 src/backends/native/meta-kms-impl-device.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/backends/native/meta-kms-impl-device.c b/src/backends/native/meta-kms-impl-device.c
index 0000000..dagu0002 100644
--- a/src/backends/native/meta-kms-impl-device.c
+++ b/src/backends/native/meta-kms-impl-device.c
@@ -2103,6 +2103,14 @@ do_handle_update (MetaKmsImplDevice *impl_device,
         }
     }
 
+  /*
+   * msm / Adreno: never poll/register the Cogl sync_fd. The atomic
+   * path only ever attaches a signaled dummy IN_FENCE when DISABLE
+   * is set; waiting here only stalls drmHandleEvent.
+   */
+  meta_kms_impl_device_update_ready (thread_impl, crtc_frame, NULL);
+  return;
+
   if (sync_fd < 0 ||
       is_fd_readable (sync_fd))
     {
